From: Simon Jackson <simon@local>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: reset Glymur xHCI after system resume

Glymur xHCI restores stale DMA ring state after system suspend. The first
DMA after resume faults the SMMU, then the host controller stops responding.

Tell xHCI that its state was lost on Glymur so it uses the existing reset
and device re-enumeration path. Do not reinitialize the parent DWC3 core or
its shared PHY clocks.
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
index 09a775b9d44d..696f58bcdd53 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
@@ -110,6 +110,7 @@ int dwc3_host_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 {
 	struct property_entry	props[6];
 	struct platform_device	*xhci;
+	struct xhci_plat_priv	priv = dwc3_xhci_plat_quirk;
 	int			ret, irq;
 	int			prop_idx = 0;
 
@@ -168,7 +169,12 @@ int dwc3_host_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 		}
 	}
 
-	ret = platform_device_add_data(xhci, &dwc3_xhci_plat_quirk,
+	priv.power_lost =
+		of_device_is_compatible(dwc->dev->of_node,
+					"qcom,glymur-dwc3") ||
+		of_device_is_compatible(dwc->dev->of_node,
+					"qcom,glymur-dwc3-mp");
+	ret = platform_device_add_data(xhci, &priv,
 				       sizeof(struct xhci_plat_priv));
 	if (ret)
 		goto err;
-- 
